    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite passes (1 run, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation, following the codebase's existing pattern for derived owner attributes (like `locality`, `contactPreference`, `membershipLevel`).\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 the DTOs are generated from this spec at build time:\n- Added `birthDate` (optional, `format: date`) to the request schema `OwnerFields`.\n- Added `ageBand` (read-only string enum `MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the response schema `Owner`.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`**:\n- Added the `birthDate` persistent field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with getter/setter.\n- Added the derived `getAgeBand()` \u2014 a small, single-responsibility getter that computes whole years between `birthDate` and `registrationDate` via `Period.between(...)` and classifies as `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), or `SENIOR` (65+), returning `null` when either date is absent (so the field is simply omitted).\n\n**Schema files** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`): added a `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in every dialect.\n\nThe wiring needed no controller/mapper changes: MapStruct maps `birthDate` from the request DTO onto the entity, and maps the derived `getAgeBand()` string onto the response DTO's enum (via `Enum.valueOf`), exactly as it already does for `contactPreference`. Since `getAgeBand()` is computed against `registrationDate`, it correctly uses the business-day-adjusted registration date resolved at persist time.",
